PROPERTY  THICKNESS     # Thickness of photocathode as function of Z position
#20 nm - Motta's best fit (ETL PMTs are used in their paper) NIM A 539 (2005) 217
#26 nm - typical of M.D.Lay meas.; Z=188_mm is 20" top  (citation needed)
#30 nm - 3-inch R12199-02 PMTs (private communication with Hamamatsu through O. Kalekin)
#The value may vary from PMT to PMT and along PMT surface. The official measurements/technical reports are not provided, 30 nm is chosen as reference
# UNITS  mm mm
#188 20e-6                 #20 nm is Motta's best fit
  188 30e-6               # 26 nm typical of M.D.Lay meas.; Z=188_mm is 20" top
# 117 26e-6               # Z=116.7_mm is start of 20" torus section
# 99  26e-6               # Z=99.0_mm is end of 17" active photocathode
# 75  26e-6               # Z=75.0_mm is 8" PMT top
# 51  26e-6               # Z=50.8_mm is 5" PMT top
  0   30e-6               # Z=0 is equator; no data for thickness, assumed same
#0   20e-6
#
# Note that, at present, all PMTs use same "photocathode" properties;
# this will have to change if we ever really want to have thickness as a
# function of Z, which would have to be tailored according to PMT type
# if you have more than one type of PMT in your detector.

